# Line endings.
#
# Development happens on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text
# files to CRLF on checkout. That is harmless for source we compile, and fatal
# for anything Linux executes directly: a shell script checked out with CRLF
# fails inside the container as
#
#     /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh: /bin/sh^M: bad interpreter
#
# and the API never starts. The entrypoint applies migrations and prepares the
# storage volume, so that is a total outage from a setting nobody touched.
#
# `* text=auto` normalises to LF in the repository; the entries below pin the
# files that must stay LF in the working tree as well.
* text=auto

*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# SQL migrations are read by Postgres, never executed as scripts, but keeping
# them LF means a diff never shows a whole file as changed after a clone.
*.sql           text eol=lf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.webp          binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
